invariant: INV-14
file: src/base64_codec.c
catches: jws_test
reason: base64url_decode no longer refuses a last group that sets a bit
  past its bytes. "Zg" and "Zh" then decode to the same byte, so one
  signature has several texts (RFC 4648 section 3.5). A caller that
  compares or stores tokens as text, such as a list of revoked tokens,
  then misses a token whose last character was changed. Every canonical
  text decodes as before. bin/jws_test requires CH_EINVAL for "Zh" and
  for "Zm9".

--- old
        bad |= tail == 3 ? (bits & 0xffU) : (bits & 0xffffU);
--- new
        bad |= 0U;
